cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Glassbox in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Glassbox: telemetry-driven differentiable vehicle dynamics identification"
authors:
  - family-names: Lillibridge
    given-names: Ryland
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-09-04
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Rylandl/glassbox"
abstract: >-
  Glassbox turns multirotor and fixed-wing telemetry into one canonical flight
  object and fits a differentiable rigid-body model whose free parameters are
  the map from actuator behaviour to forces and torques. The fitted artifact is
  a dynamics belief: one executable model, the accumulated information saying
  which of its coefficients the evidence resolved and how precisely, and the
  held-out forecast-error envelope saying how wrong its predictions have been.
  A recursive information update keeps that belief current from live telemetry
  without a proposal, a validation split or an acceptance threshold, and one
  bounded model-predictive solver turns it into a command every control
  interval, for a vehicle with a fitted model and for a vehicle with none.
keywords:
  - system identification
  - differentiable dynamics
  - uncertainty quantification
  - JAX
  - PX4
  - model predictive control
